Subject: [PATCH 5/9] NTimeDiagonalizer: the budget field and the writers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`qy_mid_run`: from the middle writer's entry on an escape's tapes, the middle writer halts
within `qyMidB` steps with the output `false :: ⟨⟨bits (g n), α⟩, 1^{n+1}⟩` (`g`'s input call,
then the three emissions of the private emitter `qyEmitTM`). `qy_top_run`: from the top writer's entry
with `1^{X - 1}` on tape 4, it halts within `qyTopB` steps with `true :: ⟨⟨bits (X²), α⟩, 1^a⟩`
(the square's install call, then the emissions). The words are `qy_writer_word`
(`pairEncode_eq` twice); a halting hosted phase is `qy_hosted_halt`. The Implementation status
paragraph records the writers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
